{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cek615LLpv9BYVNadGzwr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This matches the recent commit history shown (43e45eb94, immediately preceding the fix), confirming this is a fresh feature addition where the boundary was mistakenly set to include 0xFEFF (the BOM/ZWNBSP marker) in the RTL range.\n\n## Bug-Introducing Commits\nBIC: 43e45eb94e1aa0d1c4dbd10e99df8e366f637261\n\n## Reasoning\n(1) I traced the history of `core/java/android/text/TextUtils.java` with `git log -p` looking for the introduction of the `0xFE70`/`0xFEFF` range check that the fix commit modifies. There is exactly one prior occurrence of this line.\n\n(2) Commit `43e45eb94` (\"Adds RTL (Right-To-Left) support for all RTL languages...\") introduced the `isRTLCharacter`-style range check with `(c >= 0xFE70 && c <= 0xFEFF)`, which incorrectly includes the special Unicode marker `U+FEFF` (BOM / zero-width no-break space) as an RTL character.\n\n(3) The fix commit `137ce13f7` changes only that single line, narrowing the upper bound from `0xFEFF` to `0xFEFE`, exactly reversing the erroneous inclusion of `0xFEFF` that was added in `43e45eb94`. The commit is also the immediate parent-adjacent commit in the log (two commits prior, with a merge in between), and no other commit touched this line in between, so there's high confidence this is the sole bug-introducing commit."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":634,"cache_read_input_tokens":13317,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":634},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ae643536-bbef-45c3-b448-5cabb3da12f8","uuid":"005c8671-a2aa-4ab0-80c5-35f9616b8894","timestamp":"2026-09-05T09:52:12.327Z","request_id":"req_011Cek614cS1o4MAxZnDP7bo"}
